{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob lifted his feet.</b> The verse intends by this that he was poor and had nothing to lift except his feet. Therefore, whatever would come into his possession would be presumed to be untithed wealth, and he would be obligated to tithe two tithes from it, as he said: ״עַשֵּׂר אֲעַשְּׂרֶנּוּ״, and they of blessed memory said (Ketubot 50a): the second tithe is like the first tithe — and this is the fifth part." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that he had no need to walk — he merely lifted his feet, and immediately the land of the children of the east came to him. Therefore it did not say ״to the land of the children of the east״:" "<b>And the reason</b> the verse says <b>children of the east</b> and does not say Ḥaran, is that Ḥaran did not present itself to him — only the land of the children of the east, in which the city of Ḥaran was located. And this was from HaShem, so that Rachel would present herself to him there, and he would know what he learned there from her — and all that transpired between them, according to their words of blessed memory (Megillah 13a)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:26.781125578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}